{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_m2wlckfnjzcm7essjbwhf3kjxylk437do3ko2jf4lqt44q2orzza","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What I found and fixed\n\nThe translation was already structurally complete (28/28 symbols), but had **real byte-level divergences**:\n\n**1. NaN payload selection (the main bug class).** The C is built at `-O0`, and x86 `ADDSS/MULSS/SUBSS/DIVSS` return the *destination* operand when both operands are NaN. GCC's choice of which source-level term lands in the destination register varies per expression. I disassembled the C `.so` and transcribed the destination-first operand order for all 65 arithmetic sites, routing them through `addss`/`subss`/`mulss`/`divss` helpers that reproduce Intel's NaN rules (including SNaN quieting and the `0xFFC00000` indefinite QNaN). The previous code documented this as an unfixable divergence; it was fixable.\n\n**2. A harness bug that made everything a false pass.** `cargo test` does **not** build a `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` lib target, so the tests were `dlopen`ing a stale `.so` from an earlier `cargo build`. My first \"all green\" run was meaningless. The harness now builds the cdylib explicitly into a separate `--target-dir`.\n\n**3. The C `.so` has an undefined `sqrtf`** (CMake never links `m`). A debug test binary happens to link libm so it works by accident; a release one fails with `undefined symbol: sqrtf`. Fixed by preloading libm with `RTLD_GLOBAL` — and the handle must be *leaked*, since dropping it `dlclose`s and undoes the fix.\n\n## Making the suite prove itself\n\nPassing tests aren't evidence, so I mutation-tested the suite. It initially **missed 4 mutations**. Investigating each:\n\n- `c2RaytoAABB`'s `out->t` NaN order in the `t3` branch — a **genuine blind spot**; closed with a new NaN/infinity operand-matrix test file.\n- `c2MulmvT`'s four `mulss` orders — **genuine gap**: I'd fed its vector argument a NaN-free alphabet.\n- Two others turned out to be *provable equivalences*, not gaps: only the `else` branch can select a NaN `t_k` (NaN compares false against everything), and reaching the capsule's side-plane branch forces the relevant operands non-NaN. A 20M-case targeted search found no witness, consistent with the proof.\n\n`operand_order_check.py` now swaps every arithmetic operand pair: **46 caught, 19 provably unobservable** (each justified in the source). No `subss`/`divss` site is unobservable, which also proves every arithmetic site is reachable. `mutation_check.sh` catches **27/27 observable** behavioural mutations; 2 are documented as unobservable because `poly_ray` takes no arguments and both hard-coded rays miss (`0 << 1 == 0`) — the C can't distinguish them either.\n\n## Final state\n\n95 tests across 7 files, green under all 3 feature combinations × debug and release `.so` profiles (`verify_all.sh` exit 0). Symbol diff empty; no non-libc undefined symbols. Every `ERRORS.md` row (57) and `CONFIGS.md` row (48) has a passing differential test.\n\nTwo caveats worth flagging: the NaN-payload work is pinned to this specific GCC `-O0` build (the task's prescribed build; a `-O2` or clang build could legitimately choose different payloads), and I twice reported clean by grepping output instead of checking exit codes — the second time it hid a compile error for several minutes. `c_src/` is unmodified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1258,"cache_read_input_tokens":421791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1258,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7f5ddbc-08b7-475f-b88b-e2f573c46cbe","uuid":"7b23c99f-16fb-4e44-acb6-04e589b2a1c3","timestamp":"2026-08-27T15:10:21.850Z"}
